## 2. Product Hunt

Submit page: https://www.producthunt.com/posts/new (log in first). Launch guide: https://www.producthunt.com/launch

- **Name:** Principles Before Personalities
- **Tagline (60 characters max):** A free, offline reader for the 1939 Big Book  *(44 characters)*
- **Description (260 characters max):**
  A quiet reader for the public-domain 1939 Big Book with meeting page numbers. Highlight, mark pages, add sticky notes and search. No account, no network, nothing uploaded. Free for Mac, Windows, Android and iPhone (web app). Not affiliated with AA World Services.
  *(check the counter when you paste; trim "quiet" if it's over)*
- **Topics:** Books, Productivity, Privacy, Health
- **Pricing:** Free
- **Maker's first comment:**
  > Hi, I'm James. I built Principles Before Personalities because I wanted to read and mark up the Big Book the way I do with a paper copy, without an account or anything leaving my device.
  >
  > It ships the 1939 first edition, which is in the public domain in the US, so it's free to share. It is not the current edition. The page numbers match the ones read in meetings, so "page 58" takes you to How It Works.
  >
  > What it does: five-color highlighter and eraser, marked pages, sticky notes, full-text search, and import of your own .txt/.md files. It works offline, and highlights and notes are saved only on your device. There are no analytics in the app or on the site.
  >
  > The downloads aren't from an app store, so macOS, Windows and Android will ask you to confirm the first time. The iPhone version is a web app you add to your Home Screen from Safari.
  >
  > It's an independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Alcoholics Anonymous World Services, Inc. Feedback welcome, especially on the reading experience.

