## 3. Show HN (Hacker News)

Submit page: https://news.ycombinator.com/submit. Read the rules first: https://news.ycombinator.com/showhn.html
Post it as a normal Show HN: the title and the URL, then add the text below as your first comment. Aim it at privacy and offline software, not at recovery groups.

- **Title (80 characters max):** Show HN: An offline, no-account reader for a public-domain 1939 book  *(70)*
  Alternative: Show HN: Principles Before Personalities, a local-only reader for the 1939 Big Book  *(80)*
- **URL:** https://principles-before-personalities.netlify.app/
- **First comment:**
  > I made a small reader app for the 1939 first edition of *Alcoholics Anonymous* (the "Big Book"). That edition is in the public domain in the US. It's free, and I'm an independent developer, not affiliated with or endorsed by Alcoholics Anonymous World Services, Inc.
  >
  > The design goal was "a paper copy with a pen": highlight in five colors, mark pages, put sticky notes on a page, search the text. The constraint was that none of it should need an account or leave the device. There's no network code for user data and no telemetry, and the website is plain HTML/CSS with no scripts, cookies or trackers.
  >
  > Some implementation details:
  > - One `library.json` (~640 KB) holds all the content and drives every platform.
  > - The text is paginated to the page numbers people use in meetings, so you can jump straight to "page 58".
  > - Mac is native SwiftUI (macOS 14+). Windows is a .NET Framework 4.6.2 desktop app. Android is a sideloaded .apk. iPhone is a PWA with a service worker, because a native App Store build needs Apple's paid developer program.
  > - Highlights merge and split on overlap, and there's an eraser. You can import your own .txt/.md files, which get split into chapters and pages.
  >
  > The builds aren't signed or from a store, so expect Gatekeeper, SmartScreen and "unknown apps" prompts the first time. I'd like to hear what you think of the local-storage approach and the PWA's offline behaviour.
  >
  > *[If the source is public, add: "Code: <repo URL>". Don't claim it's open source unless it is.]*

