## 5. Outreach email to recovery bloggers and podcasters

Send only to people whose site or show already covers recovery tools or reading, one at a time, personalized. Don't mass-mail. If someone doesn't reply, leave it there.

**Subject:** A free, offline reader for the 1939 Big Book (for your recovery tools list)

> Hi [Name],
>
> I've read [specific post or episode], especially [one specific thing you liked], and thought you might want to know about a small free tool I made.
>
> Principles Before Personalities is a reader for the public-domain 1939 first edition of the Big Book. It uses the page numbers read in meetings, and you can highlight, mark pages, leave sticky notes and search. There's no account, it works offline, and nothing you write is uploaded. It runs on Mac, Windows, Android and iPhone (as a web app added from Safari). It's completely free.
>
> https://principles-before-personalities.netlify.app/
>
> To be clear about what it isn't: it's the 1939 text, not the current edition, and it's an independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Alcoholics Anonymous World Services, Inc.
>
> If it seems useful for your readers or listeners, feel free to mention it. If not, no reply needed. Happy to answer any questions.
>
> Thanks for the work you do,
> James Murphy

