## 6. Subreddit weekly resource or self-promotion threads

**Check each subreddit's rules and sidebar first**, and post only in a thread that explicitly allows resources or self-promotion. Many recovery subs ban promotion completely. Don't post it as a new thread, and don't drop the link into anyone's personal share. Rules pages (checked 2026-09-25): r/alcoholicsanonymous https://www.reddit.com/r/alcoholicsanonymous/about/rules/ · r/stopdrinking wiki https://www.reddit.com/r/stopdrinking/wiki/index · r/redditorsinrecovery https://www.reddit.com/r/redditorsinrecovery/about/rules/. If a sub has no such thread, don't post there. You could message the mods and ask, once.

**Reply text:**

> I made a free reader for the 1939 first edition of the Big Book, which is in the public domain. It keeps the page numbers we read in meetings, so you can jump to a page, and you can highlight, mark pages and leave sticky notes like you would in a paper copy. No account, works offline, and your notes stay on your phone or computer. Mac, Windows, Android, and iPhone (as a web app from Safari).
>
> https://principles-before-personalities.netlify.app/
>
> It's the 1939 text, not the current edition. Not affiliated with or endorsed by Alcoholics Anonymous World Services, Inc. Just something I built for my own reading and wanted to share.

